{"id": "SGU_Episode_665", "title": "SGU Episode 665", "type": "structured", "description": "The Skeptic's Guide to the Universe, Episode 665 Transcript", "metadata": {"title": "SGU Episode 665", "date": "April 7 2024", "year": 2024, "month": 4, "day": 7, "rogues": ["Steven Novella", "Jay Novella", "Evan Bernstein", "Bob Novella", "Cara Santa Maria"], "quotee_url": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plato", "quote": "\n Do not train children to learning by force and harshness, but direct them to it by what amuses their minds, so that you may be better able to discover with accuracy the peculiar bent of the genius of each. \n", "quotee": "\n Plato  ( The Republic )\n", "quotee_title": "", "guests": [{"guest": "Mark Lynas", "guest_title": " British author", "guest_url": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Lynas"}], "categories": [], "podcast_url": "https://www.theskepticsguide.org/podcasts/episode-665", "episode_number": 665}, "sections": [{"id": 0, "text": "Voice-over: You're listening to the Skeptics' Guide to the Universe, your escape to reality.\n\n[v 1][v 2]\n\nclay licks\n", "title": "Introduction, Cara back from the Amazon", "metadata": {"title": "Introduction, Cara back from the Amazon"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 1, "text": "Atavism[v 3]", "title": "What's the Word", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:07:20", "hour": 0, "minute": "7", "second": "20", "title": "What's the Word"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 2, "text": "", "title": "News Items", "metadata": {"title": "News Items"}, "sections": [{"id": 3, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 4, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "B", "speaker": "Bob Novella"}}, {"id": 5, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "C", "speaker": "Cara Santa Maria"}}, {"id": 6, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "J", "speaker": "Jay Novella"}}, {"id": 7, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 8, "text": "(laughs)\n(laughter)\n(applause)\n[inaudible]", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 9, "text": "\nThe Nation indulges in fear mongering about cell phones and cancer\u00a0[1]\n\n\n", "title": "Cell Phones and Cancer", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:13:43", "hour": 0, "minute": "13", "second": "43", "links": ["https://sciencebasedmedicine.org/the-nation-indulges-in-some-particularly-egregious-fear-mongering-about-cell-phones-and-cancer/"], "title": "Cell Phones and Cancer"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 10, "text": "\nNASA funds project to study feasibility of using robot bees to study Mars from a new perspective\u00a0[2]\n\n\n", "title": "Robot Bees on Mars", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:27:08", "hour": 0, "minute": "27", "second": "08", "links": ["https://phys.org/news/2018-04-nasa-funds-feasibility-robot-bees.html"], "title": "Robot Bees on Mars"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 11, "text": "\nHuge Dinosaur Footprints Discovered on Scottish Coast\u00a0[3]\n\n\n", "title": "Largest Dinosaurs", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:35:16", "hour": 0, "minute": "35", "second": "16", "links": ["https://web.archive.org/web/20180617092932/https://news.nationalgeographic.com/2018/04/sauropods-dinosaurs-footprints-scotland-fossils-science/"], "title": "Largest Dinosaurs"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 12, "text": "", "title": "Who's That Noisy?", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:42:48", "hour": 0, "minute": "42", "second": "48", "title": "Who's That Noisy?"}, "sections": [{"id": 13, "text": "[Groaning animal cries and braying]\n\nshort_text_from_transcript\n", "title": "New Noisy", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:45:55", "hour": 0, "minute": "45", "second": "55", "title": "New Noisy"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 14, "text": "", "title": "Questions and Emails", "metadata": {"title": "Questions and Emails"}, "sections": [{"id": 15, "text": "F of Y/F \u2013 1 = Y/((1-.3)*Y) \u2013 1 = 1/.7 \u2013 1 = 42.9%.", "title": "Correction: Math Correction", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:48:30", "hour": 0, "minute": "48", "second": "30", "title": "Correction: Math Correction"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 16, "text": "Neurologica: Science and Pseudoscience of the Interstitium", "title": "Followup: Interstitium", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:49:31", "hour": 0, "minute": "49", "second": "31", "links": ["https://theness.com/neurologicablog/index.php/science-and-pseudoscience-of-the-interstitium/"], "title": "Followup: Interstitium"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 17, "text": "Mark Lynas, scientific environmentalist and eco-activist", "title": "Interview with Mark Lynas", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:58:11", "hour": 0, "minute": "58", "second": "11", "links": ["http://www.marklynas.org/"], "title": "Interview with Mark Lynas"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 18, "text": "Voice-over: It's time for Science or Fiction.\n", "title": "Science or Fiction", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:22:05", "hour": "1", "minute": "22", "second": "05", "title": "Science or Fiction"}, "sections": [{"id": 19, "text": "", "title": "Jay's Response", "metadata": {"title": "Jay's Response"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 20, "text": "", "title": "Bob's Response", "metadata": {"title": "Bob's Response"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 21, "text": "", "title": "Evan's Response", "metadata": {"title": "Evan's Response"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 22, "text": "", "title": "Cara's Response", "metadata": {"title": "Cara's Response"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 23, "text": "", "title": "Steve Explains Item #1", "metadata": {"title": "Steve Explains Item #1"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 24, "text": "", "title": "Steve Explains Item #2", "metadata": {"title": "Steve Explains Item #2"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 25, "text": "", "title": "Steve Explains Item #3", "metadata": {"title": "Steve Explains Item #3"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 26, "text": "", "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:34:13", "hour": "1", "minute": "34", "second": "13", "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 27, "text": "", "title": "Announcements", "metadata": {"title": "Announcements"}, "sections": [{"id": 28, "text": "", "title": "Book Progress", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:34:42", "hour": "1", "minute": "34", "second": "42", "title": "Book Progress"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 29, "text": "", "title": "NECSS 2018", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:38:39", "hour": "1", "minute": "38", "second": "39", "title": "NECSS 2018"}, "sections": [{"id": 30, "text": "Skeptics' Guide to the Universe is produced by SGU Productions, dedicated to promoting science and critical thinking. For more information, visit us at theskepticsguide.org. Send your questions to info@theskepticsguide.org. And, if you would like to support the show and all the work that we do, go to patreon.com/SkepticsGuide and consider becoming a patron and becoming part of the SGU community. Our listeners and supporters are what make SGU possible.", "metadata": {"links": ["http://www.theskepticsguide.org", "https://www.patreon.com/SkepticsGuide"], "speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}]}]}, {"id": 31, "text": "", "title": "Today I Learned", "metadata": {"title": "Today I Learned"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 32, "text": "\n\u2191 Science-Based Medicine: The Nation indulges in fear mongering about cell phones and cancer\n\n\u2191 NASA: NASA funds project to study feasibility of using robot bees to study Mars from a new perspective\n\n\u2191 National Geographic: Huge Dinosaur Footprints Discovered on Scottish Coast\n\n\u2191 Britannica:\u00a0pirarucu\n\n\u2191 NatGeo: These Spiders Build Decoy Dummies of Themselves\n\n\u2191 Wired (article 6 years older than NatGeo video):\u00a0Spider That Builds Its Own Spider Decoys Discovered\n\n\u2191 Dolphinspedia:\u00a0Why Are Pink Dolphins Pink?\n\n\u2191 [url_for_TIL publication: title]\n\n", "title": "References", "metadata": {"links": ["https://sciencebasedmedicine.org/the-nation-indulges-in-some-particularly-egregious-fear-mongering-about-cell-phones-and-cancer/", "https://phys.org/news/2018-04-nasa-funds-feasibility-robot-bees.html", "https://web.archive.org/web/20180617092932/https://news.nationalgeographic.com/2018/04/sauropods-dinosaurs-footprints-scotland-fossils-science/", "https://www.britannica.com/animal/pirarucu", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ce7hWBivPFM", "https://www.wired.com/2012/12/spider-building-spider/", "https://web.archive.org/web/20181202222237/http://dolphinspedia.com/dolphins-facts/why-are-pink-dolphins-pink/#.XARbNC-l0cg"], "title": "References"}, "sections": [{"id": 33, "text": "\n\u2191 Spanish Wikipedia: friaje\n\n\u2191 Journal of Herpetology: Extreme Weather Events and the Vertical Microhabitat of Rain Forest Anurans\n\n\u2191 Wiktionary: atavism\n\n", "title": "Vocabulary", "metadata": {"links": ["https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friaje", "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1565781", "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/atavism"], "title": "Vocabulary"}, "sections": []}]}]}